 "id": "setting/effort-change/break-from-messages",
 "description": "A router lowers the effort of request 5 from high to low, on the same large-model. On a model that does not render the effort ahead of the messages (cached-prefix.md), the tools and the system stay valid: the provider reads 8,000 tokens and writes the 32,000 tokens of messages 0 to 3 again. The two bodies are identical up to the new message, so a body comparison finds nothing; the setting carries its position, messages[0]. 32,000 x ($3.75 - $0.30) = -$0.11040.",
 "source": "examples.md#5b",
